---
title: Map
layout: base.njk
map: true
# LOCAL ONLY. The permalink is decided in src/map.11tydata.js, which returns
# false on a Cloudflare build — so this page is not written, not linked and
# not deployed. It exists at http://localhost:8080/map/ under `npm run dev`
# and nowhere else.
#
# To publish it when it is ready: add `navLabel: map` and `navOrder: 3` here,
# then follow the note in src/map.11tydata.js.
noindex: true
description: Where every*one is happening — every venue in the Adelaide Design Week 2026 program, on one map of Kaurna/Adelaide.
---

<header class="pg-head map-head">
<h1 class="pg-h1">Map</h1>
<p class="pg-intro">{{ mapPoints.eventCount }} events across {{ mapPoints.venueCount }} places. Tap an <svg class="ast ast--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#ast"></use></svg> to see what is on there.</p>
</header>

{% if env.mapboxToken %}

<div class="map-wrap">

  <div id="adw-map" class="map-canvas" role="application" aria-label="Map of Adelaide Design Week venues">
    {# Shown only if the basemap never arrives. The list beside it is
       unaffected, so the page is still usable — say that, rather than
       leaving a blank rectangle to be interpreted. #}
    <p class="map-stalled">The map could not load. Everything is still listed{% if mapPoints.venues.length %} on the right{% endif %} — and refreshing usually fixes it.</p>
  </div>

  {# The list is the map's equal, not its caption. Mapbox draws its markers to
     a canvas where they cannot be tabbed to or read aloud, so everything the
     markers do is also reachable here — which happens to be what most people
     want anyway: a list they can read down. #}
  <aside class="map-side" id="adw-map-side" aria-label="Venues and shows">

    {# The same controls the program page uses, and the same classes, so the
       two pages are visibly one system. Inventing a second set of buttons
       here is what made this look like a different site. #}
    <div class="map-side-controls">
      <div class="pg-views" role="tablist" aria-label="Show list of">
        <button class="pg-view is-on" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true"
                data-mode="venues">venues</button>
        <button class="pg-view" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
                data-mode="shows">shows</button>
      </div>

      <div class="pg-days map-days" role="group" aria-label="Filter by day">
        <button class="pg-daybtn is-on" type="button" data-day="" aria-pressed="true">all</button>
        {%- for d in mapPoints.days %}
        <button class="pg-daybtn" type="button" data-day="{{ d }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ d }}</button>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="map-side-count" id="adw-map-count" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="map-side-list" id="adw-map-list"></div>

    <div class="map-side-detail" id="adw-map-detail" hidden>
      <button type="button" class="map-detail-back">&larr; back to the list</button>
      <div class="map-detail-body"></div>
    </div>

  </aside>

</div>

<div class="map-legend">
  <h2 class="map-legend-h">the marks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-exh" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> exhibition</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-conv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> conversation</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-inst" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> installation</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-open" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> open studio</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-tour" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> tour</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-work" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> workshop</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="map-legend-note">A bigger <svg class="ast ast--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#ast"></use></svg> with a number is several events together — tap it to open them up.</p>
</div>

{# Parsed by map.js. A script tag of type application/json is inert: the
   browser never executes it, so event titles and blurbs cannot escape into
   the page as code. #}
<script type="application/json" id="adw-map-data">{{ { "token": env.mapboxToken, "style": site.mapboxStyle, "geojson": mapPoints.geojson, "circuit": mapPoints.circuit } | dump | safe }}</script>

{% else %}

{# A missing token is the most likely reason this page is not a map, and
   "it did not work" is not a useful thing for it to say. Name the variable,
   the place it goes, and the thing people forget — that Cloudflare reads
   variables at build time, so adding one changes nothing until a rebuild. #}
<div class="page prose">
  <p><strong>The map is not switched on yet.</strong> This build had no Mapbox token.</p>
  <p>Built {% if env.branch %}on Cloudflare, branch <code>{{ env.branch }}</code>{% else %}locally{% endif %}. It needs a public token (starting <code>pk.</code>) in <code>MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN</code>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Locally</strong> — copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code>, fill it in, restart <code>npm run dev</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>On Cloudflare Pages</strong> — Settings → Environment variables → <strong>Preview</strong> (a variable set only under Production will not reach this branch) → <code>MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN</code>. Then <strong>redeploy</strong>: Cloudflare reads variables when it builds, so adding one has no effect until the next build.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The token also has to allow this hostname. In Mapbox, its URL restrictions must include <code>https://{{ env.branch or "localhost" }}{% if env.branch %}.adw-website.pages.dev{% endif %}/*</code>, or tiles come back 403 and the map is blank.</p>
</div>

{% endif %}

{% if mapPoints.dropped.length %}
{# Visible to editors reading the page source, not to visitors. A venue that
   quietly fails to appear is the failure mode worth making noisy. #}
<!--
  Not on the map ({{ mapPoints.dropped.length }}):
  {%- for d in mapPoints.dropped %}
  - {{ d.title }} @ {{ d.venue }} — {{ d.reason }}
  {%- endfor %}
-->
{% endif %}
